The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
virtio_config_disable(dev);
ret = drv->freeze(dev);
```
Reason:
The device configuration is disabled when attempting to freeze the device, and if the freezing operation fails (indicated by a non-zero return value), the configuration remains disabled. This prevents the device from responding to resize requests, as it does not receive notifications about configuration changes.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (ret) {
    virtio_config_enable(dev);
}
```
Reason:
This code re-enables the device configuration if the attempt to freeze the device fails. By restoring the configuration, the device can once again respond to resize requests and receive notifications about configuration changes, thus restoring its expected functionality.

